What was changed:
  - The PyTorch checkpoint was exported to ONNX (opset 17, float32) by scripts/export_maia3.py.
    The weights are not changed, retrained or quantised. RMSNorm is written out as
    ReduceMean/Sqrt/Div/Mul because the exporter has no RMSNorm operator.
  - The exported graph returns the move policy and value logits only; the ponder (time) head
    output is dropped.
  - backend/bots/maia.py re-implements the upstream input encoding (maia3/dataset.py,
    tokenize_board and get_historical_tokens) with numpy instead of torch.
